    "created_at": "2025-05-16T12:26:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-16T12:30:54Z",
    "body": "> The `Location` header is a completely separate topic, so I'm going to be marking your comment as off-topic as well. That issue is also too long to understand in a reasonable amount of time. I suspect you need at least [#601](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/601) though. If you think you need more, please file a dedicated issue with a clear description.\n\nI try to clarify what stof is talking about:\n1. Turbo uses `fetch` to make a Request to the server\n2. The server responds with a redirect (3XX) and a Location header including a fragment (e.g. `Location: /path#anchor`)\n3. Turbo redirects to `/path`, as there is no way to get the fragment (`#anchor`)\n\nSo adding a new property, e.g. `Response.prototype.hash` like @annevk proposed in https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/1167#issuecomment-2830134900, would make it possible to fix it in future Turbo versions in a backwards compatible manner.\n\nChanging `Response.prototype.url` to include the fragment could probably lead to broken existing code. So there is no way to implement a fix which would affect the current version of Turbo. So if this proposal would be implemented in all Browsers Turbo would require an update to support redirects to a specific anchor.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
